WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:02.936
 Dan, Randy, when
you came here,

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.637
we asked you to
make fantasy blades.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.073
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.409
to make this fantastic weapon.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.948
Attila the Hun's Sword of Mars.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.417
 [chukles]

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.786
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.221 line:7%
[metal music]

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.290 line:0%
RANDY: I'm back
at my home forge,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.327 line:0%
and I'm gonna be making
sword out of Damascus.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:31.297
I'm making it Damascus to
catch the judge's eyes.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.066
Damscus, you can have
all kinds of problems.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.903
It could fail on me, but
I'm gonna take a chance

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.339
and see where this
one comes out.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:45.045
I'm stretching my bit out, and
I cut it in six equal pieces.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:48.147
Now I'm welding it back
together to go back in the forge

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.083
and forge weld it
and stretch it out.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:53.553
I'll have 78 layers when I
get through, and hopefully,

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.188
a pretty pattern.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:59.058
If it sets weld, I'm home
free, but I hope it holds.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.226
It's scrap.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.895
The weld didn't hold.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:02.995
It's got a point.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.731
I'm afraid if I keep
fooling with it,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:08.034
I'm gonna run out
of metal, so I'm

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.004
gonna scrap it, start all over.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:15.608
I got 3 and 1/2
hours of dead nut--

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:19.745
Mars going really be what
makes or breaks the deal.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.147 line:7%
I'm gonna have to push it.

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:23.516 line:7%
 Just the start of day two.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.184 line:0%
I want to get the heat treat
and temper out of the way

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.186 line:0%
and done so I can start
working on the finer

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.588 line:7%
details of this blade.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:29.856
This one's for the money.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.425
There's a lot of concerns when
you make a blade this long,

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:34.427
because if you don't
have it even in flat,

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:38.831
that gives it more of a
chance to warp in the clinch.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.534
I pull it out of the oil,
the blade's got a slight warp

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.236
in it, but it's hard.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:48.507
I still have enough time to bend
it, just a very small window.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.110
And then I'm there
holding two blades.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.212
Dammit, this sucks.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.047
There goes almost
a full day of work.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.716
Time is of the essence.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.686
I've going to get started
on another blade, now.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.588 line:7%
This is really going to suck.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:06.326 line:0%
 On day two, I got my
new blade stretched out.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:10.163 line:0%
I wound up with 13
layers instead of 78.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:13.966
Today, I'm starting
off fitting these ball

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.203
spindles to my guard.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:22.174
I got my ball spindle
made, just don't look good.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.311
I struggled to get it
this far, but I believe

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:27.246
I'm going to start it
all over, because it

00:02:27.312 --> 00:02:29.382
just got too much space in it.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:32.351
This guard is kind
of getting to me.

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:35.721
It's really beginning
to get on my nerves.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.389
It's time to trash this.

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:39.959 line:0%
I need this to
work, because if it

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.361 line:0%
don't, I don't
know that I'll have

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:45.197 line:7%
enough time to start all over.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:46.232 line:7%
 It's the start of day four.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.833 line:7%
I lost time with my first blade.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.235
Time's winding down now.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.771
I want to make sure that this
is spot-on for the judges.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:55.641
Tang's a little thin,
but should be working.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:59.078
Now I'm going to start work
on my handle, which is going

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.413
to be made of this
little dolphin

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:01.981
that I got from a thrift store.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.783
I like to find a
use for everything.

00:03:06.151 --> 00:03:08.287
I want to get the tang
burned in all the way.

00:03:08.353 --> 00:03:09.722 line:7%
You see how it's not smoking?

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.391 line:0%
That means the wood's not
touching any part that's hot.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.894
I couldn't get the Tang
hot enough to burn in,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.997
so the only thing keeping
me from going all the way up

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.098
is the width here.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.299
So I got to stick
it in a drill press

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:22.935
and then drill out a little bit.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.104
I fit the handle,
and epoxy it in.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.740
Once it's on there,
it's permanent.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.175
I can't go back.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:32.778
This is insanely nerve-racking.

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.848
If my fit-up is loose
whatsoever, I could go home.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.785
I wish I had more time to
make it a little bit better.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:42.755 line:7%
Oop, there goes your cushion.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.390 line:7%
 It's the last day.

00:03:44.456 --> 00:03:48.160
I've had a few setbacks,
but I'm almost done.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:52.264
I'm going to put some
jewels in the handle.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:55.268
Attila, he was a
great leader, and I

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.337
think the jewels will
be something that he

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.507
would have in his sword.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.842
I've got my jewels in it.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.077
There's one thing left
to do, etch it and see

00:04:05.143 --> 00:04:08.714
what kind of pattern I've got.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.916
Oy, yeah.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.818
The pattern turned out well.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.219
I don't believe I could
have done any better

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:15.755
if I had more layers.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.923
I think I've built
a sword that Attila

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.958
the Hun would be proud of.

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:21.361
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.729
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.965
I will deliver killing blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:27.833
Randy, you're up first.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.668
You ready?

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.168
 I am.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.603
 Let's do this.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:32.972
 I don't know what
to expect, and I know

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:34.540
they're going to hit it hard.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.342
I'm a little bit gibbery.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.977
My legs won't give out
from under me a little bit,

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:40.980
but I think I'll be OK.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.549
[dramatic music]

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.920
[metal music]

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.397
 All right.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:08.040
 All right, let's talk about
your Sword of Mars here.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:11.944
First up, the Damascus pattern
you have here is gorgeous.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.012
 Thank you.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.214
 The weapon design's very
aggressive for thrusting

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.282
and slashing.

00:05:16.348 --> 00:05:17.817
Now your handle construction.

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:21.019
If you reverse this,
it'll be easier to have

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:22.388
something to lock on to.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:24.624
The fact that the flare was
right here, forcing my hand

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.526
to open up if I want
to marry into the hilt.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.028
This is a very sharp weapon.

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:33.398
The tip pierces all the way
through, cuts on the way out.

00:05:33.465 --> 00:05:37.202
It's pointy and scary,
and it will kill.

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:38.003
 Thank you.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:38.938
 Good job.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.272
All right, Dan, it is your turn.
You ready?

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:41.040
 Hell, yeah.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.241
 Let's do this.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:43.308
 I was hoping the kill
test would be a dummy.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:45.678
I know heads will roll.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.146
I'm feeling really confident.

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.381
I want to see what
this thing does.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:51.984
[metal music]

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.507
 All right, Dan, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.342
I love the balance
of your blade.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:20.045
When I go forward, it's
not hard to pull back to go

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:21.347
in again for another kill.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:22.815
Now your handle construction.

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.917
It's curved enough
to where it doesn't

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:25.985
want to fly out of my hand.

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:27.854
It's got a good grip
and control for this.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.723
Your edge allows for very
deep cuts into the abdomen

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:32.958
right there.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:36.195
The only issue we have is that
your tip picked up a bend when

00:06:36.228 --> 00:06:37.830
it's chopped into the spine.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:40.732
But, your weapon,
sir, will kill.

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:41.534
 Thank you.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.105
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:49.741
Now, Attila's armies were
basically one large cavalry.

00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:51.210
And through his
military campaigns,

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:54.113
he revolutionized the use of
horse in military conflicts.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.482
So to test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:59.952
I'll be chopping into
these horse skulls.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:00.952
Randy, you're up first.

00:07:00.986 --> 00:07:01.753
You ready?

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:02.821
 I guess so.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.056
 OK.

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:08.093
 I designed my blade
with a sharp, sharp edge,

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.762
and I'm a little worried.

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:11.997
My stomach's up in my
throat a little bit.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.366
[dramatic music]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:19.505
[metal music]

00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:30.716
Oh.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:34.053
 OK, so right off the
bat, the biggest thing

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:39.225
is that this section from
right about here to here

00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:41.260
has lost its edge.

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:45.464
There's a couple of small rolls.

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.633
Blade's still straight,
it's all in one piece,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.101
still solid, nicely done.

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:50.268
It's a very strong blade.

00:07:50.335 --> 00:07:51.270
 Thank you.

00:07:51.336 --> 00:07:52.304
 All right, Dan, are you ready?

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:54.306
 No, but let's do it.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.375
 Everybody says that.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:58.678 line:0%
 The first test
bent my blade, so I'm

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.146 line:0%
feeling a little bit of fear
going into the strength test.

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:03.282 line:7%
This will kill blades.

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:05.050
It's a scary, brutal thing.

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:07.720
[dramatic music]

00:08:10.455 --> 00:08:15.027
[metal music]

00:08:28.907 --> 00:08:29.842
 At the guard.

00:08:33.545 --> 00:08:36.581
 OK, so before we
get to the obvious,

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:38.918
I really like the
design of your blade.

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:40.620
It's got a great
weight to it, had

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:44.290
a really good feel in my hand,
the balance was really nice.

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:47.259
See all that space
around your tang?

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:51.029
With that room for that blade
to move inside the guard,

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:55.167
it could just create so much
stress that it cut loose

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:56.502
right there at the corner.

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:58.837
If it were all tight, there
wouldn't be any stress.

00:08:58.904 --> 00:09:01.306
There's no discoloration
here, so it's not that there

00:09:01.373 --> 00:09:02.608
was a crack here before.

00:09:02.674 --> 00:09:04.042
The grain structure looks fine.

00:09:04.109 --> 00:09:06.679
It was a well-designed
piece, but obvious flaw.

00:09:09.314 --> 00:09:12.451
 Dan, unfortunately, your blade
suffered a catastrophic failure

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:14.120
in the middle of
our strength test,

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:16.989
which means that we
can no longer test it.

00:09:17.055 --> 00:09:19.025
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:21.393
shake your competitor's
hand, and then

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.362
please leave the forge.

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:25.397
 It hurts, but
my sword breaking

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:26.665
is going to be a
reminder that I have

00:09:26.731 --> 00:09:28.633
to push harder and be better.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:29.501
 Dan, keep up the work.

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:30.903
That's a good sword.

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:32.972
 I came here to prove that I
can compete with the big dogs,

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:34.407
and that I do know
what I'm doing.

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:37.910
And I think I might
have accomplished that.

00:09:37.977 --> 00:09:41.147
 Randy, the strength and
efficiency of your weapon

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:42.815
in the kill test have
earned you the title

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:46.151
of Forged in Fire Champion,
and a check for how much?

00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:47.219
 $10,000.

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.654
 That's right, $10,000.

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:49.554
Good job, brother.

00:09:49.621 --> 00:09:51.223
 I won Forged in Fire.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.257
It's reality.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.125
 How do you feel?

00:09:53.158 --> 00:09:54.193
 Good.

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:57.529
To be a champion and be
recognized as a good bladesmith

00:09:57.563 --> 00:09:59.398
is real good.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:02.301
This is my happy
and excited face--

00:10:02.367 --> 00:10:03.569
 Real good sword.

00:10:03.635 --> 00:10:05.404
 --if you didn't recognize it.

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:08.874
[metal music]

